cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal
  synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI assistant by
  Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed,
  and not a new result.
title: "reader-ergonomics-software-design"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-29
abstract: >-
  How to write the documents that design software before the code: algorithm
  specifications, design documents, decision records, architecture
  descriptions and system diagrams, with shapes, graded principles and checks
  to run in CI.
  An extension of reader-ergonomics: the evidence and document shapes
  particular to software design and the writing about it.
  Use it as a reading list and a starting point, not as an authority.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/reader-ergonomics-software-design"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - software architecture
  - system design
  - algorithm design
  - formal specification
  - design documents
  - pseudocode
  - documentation
  - literature review
